              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you own or manage a fleet in Florida, you know that keeping your trucks on the road safely is non-negotiable. One of the most crucial, and most overlooked, aspects of vehicle safety is semi truck brake maintenance.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Your brakes are your first line of defense against accidents, costly downtime, and unexpected repairs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we understand how much your trucks mean to your business. Our parts and service departments are built around helping you protect your investment, keep your drivers safe, and extend the lifespan of your equipment.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-it-matters",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Brake Maintenance Matters for Your Fleet",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-it-matters"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Brake systems on semi trucks face extreme wear and tear. Between heavy loads, long miles, and Florida's unpredictable weather, your brakes are constantly under pressure.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "stats-why-it-matters-2",
                  "type": "statBand",
                  "props": {
                    "stats": [
                      {
                        "value": "25%",
                        "label": "Of all truck out-of-service violations are brake-related, per the Commercial Vehicle Safety Alliance"
                      },
                      {
                        "value": "25,000–30,000 MI",
                        "label": "General rule of thumb for brake inspection intervals on active fleets"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "That means poor brake performance isn't just a safety hazard; it can also take your truck off the road, cutting into productivity and profits. Routine brake maintenance helps prevent:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-why-it-matters-4",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Uneven wear and costly replacements"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Increased stopping distances"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Brake fade or overheating on long hauls"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Unexpected breakdowns and roadside delays"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Your fleet can't afford that kind of downtime, and neither can your bottom line.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-signs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Signs Your Semi Truck Brakes Need Service",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "signs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Knowing when to schedule maintenance can make all the difference. Look out for these warning signs:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-signs-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Pulling to one side when braking"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Grinding or squealing noises"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Soft or spongy brake pedal feel"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Increased stopping distance"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Visible wear on brake pads, drums, or rotors"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Air leaks in pneumatic brake systems"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If any of these issues sound familiar, it's time to schedule a brake inspection at Sun State International. Our certified technicians are trained to spot small issues before they become big problems.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-florida-conditions",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Florida Driving Conditions and Brake Wear",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "florida-conditions"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-florida-conditions-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Florida's climate can be tough on trucks. High humidity, heavy rain, and coastal salt air can accelerate corrosion and rust on brake components. Add in long stretches of stop-and-go traffic or tight delivery routes, and your braking system is under constant strain. The last thing you'll want as a fleet operator is to have one of your drivers stranded on the side of the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-florida-conditions-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "That's why preventive brake maintenance isn't optional; it's essential. At Sun State International, we help fleets adapt to these local conditions with maintenance plans tailored to how and where your trucks operate.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-how-often",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Often Should You Schedule Brake Maintenance for Your Semi Trucks?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "how-often"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-how-often-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A good rule of thumb is to inspect your brakes every 25,000 to 30,000 miles, or at least twice a year for active fleets. However, your schedule may vary depending on:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-how-often-2",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Load weight and frequency"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Terrain and driving conditions"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Type of braking system (air or hydraulic)"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Driver habits"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-how-often-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Sun State International's service advisors can help you set up a custom maintenance plan that fits your fleet's schedule and keeps every truck road-ready.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-oem-vs-aftermarket",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "OEM vs. Aftermarket Brake Parts",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "oem-vs-aftermarket"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-oem-vs-aftermarket-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When it comes time to replace brake components, quality matters. Using OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) parts ensures that your trucks maintain factory-level performance, durability, and safety.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-oem-vs-aftermarket-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we carry genuine International Truck parts designed to fit your model perfectly; no guesswork, no shortcuts. Our parts specialists will help you find the right components faster, so you can get your trucks back on the road with confidence.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-oem-vs-aftermarket-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Need quality replacement parts? Visit our Parts Department to order genuine International brake parts or speak with our Tampa, Sarasota, Davenport, or Brooksville teams. If you can't make it to one of our locations, we also offer parts online so you can get what you need fast.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-oem-vs-aftermarket-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-oem-vs-aftermarket-4",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
